{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch","id":1166173,"title":"Rote Crunch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-08T15:21:48-08:00","id":1166173,"title":"Rote Crunch","content":"Been quite a while since I posted on here. I was curious how people like to give mechanical effects to their rotes.<br /> <br /> Personally I do multiple things such on simple rotes might have a -1 to difficulty or need less successes depending on what it does and for more complicated rotes I like to give them special rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T08:58:21-08:00","id":1171246,"title":"","content":"Hey, I don't know if you still care about this since your post is a bit old, but I've been thinking about letting players buy rotes for 1 XP each like in the old system and then the advantage will just be that they don't get a fast-casting penalty for using it in stressful situations. My main concern is that this runs somewhat counter to what Mage is all about, which is making up spells on the fly to suit the situation - that freedom to be wildly inventive is what I love most about the magick system, so I'm worried about encouraging a more rigid play style.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, even without this benefit I've noticed my players tend to fall back on some of the same Effects a lot - my Verbena's Life 3 / Prime 2 enchanted hand-claws, my Virtual Adept's direct Mind 3 attack... it would kind of make sense to let them buy those as rotes to use almost like signature spells. What do you think about that sort of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T16:40:51-08:00","id":1171368,"title":"","content":"Even if that's all it is then it still is something that has a mechanical effect on the game. I agree with the thought that the ability to make magic to suite your mage is what the game is all about. I was just curious as to how people make rotes important in their games. One more reason I like the concept of rotes is that I feel they are good at putting a player in the mind of the mage by making them think about how their mage performs the spell. Though I'm of the mindset that a well refined spell should have some game mechanical effect too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:02:03-08:00","id":1171406,"title":"","content":"I usually consider the Rotes like foci: something the Mage learns as a beginner, tying his belief into established rituals that give him enough confidence to pull an effect out. Through the Epiphanies (or in-game events, like improvising something without time or materials for the proper ritual) he gradually learns that whatever constraint he's putting on his reality is unnecessary, so as his Arete raises his need for Rotes lessens and he becomes more adept at improvised casting.<br /> My beginner mages (players) usually can only cast through Rotes, while the more experienced ones know they can bend reality even without them but still feel the safety of established procedures (therefore the usual -1 diff keeps existing). It depends from character to character though.<br /> <br /> Similar argument for the Technocracy, but I stress even more the need for proper Rotes and Foci there since their Technology paradigm is supposed to be more rigid than the Tradition occult pastiche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T19:13:29-08:00","id":1171413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umsakis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171246#post1171246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I don't know if you still care about this since your post is a bit old, but I've been thinking about letting players buy rotes for 1 XP each like in the old system and then the advantage will just be that they don't get a fast-casting penalty for using it in stressful situations. My main concern is that this runs somewhat counter to what Mage is all about, which is making up spells on the fly to suit the situation - that freedom to be wildly inventive is what I love most about the magick system, so I'm worried about encouraging a more rigid play style.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, even without this benefit I've noticed my players tend to fall back on some of the same Effects a lot - my Verbena's Life 3 / Prime 2 enchanted hand-claws, my Virtual Adept's direct Mind 3 attack... it would kind of make sense to let them buy those as rotes to use almost like signature spells. What do you think about that sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the simplest way of doing it, I think. I never really liked that M20 don't give real rules for rotes, since I think they are logical.<br /> <br /> Just as a parallel, take martial arts (or any kind of activity, physical or mental, really). &quot;Rotes&quot; are the things you practiced 'til they became ingrained and you can do them more quickly, reliably and under stress. M20 just doesn't handle that.<br /> <br /> That Mage's magic system's pint is the creativity? Yes, but you could be creative with designing rotes and also with spontaneous casting, if you don't have a handy rote, I don't think it takes away from the creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T01:18:53-08:00","id":1171481,"title":"","content":"Rotes I feel are important in Mage. Of all things they show what a Paradigm can do and how it works, fast casting and being able to act in the moment is great and certainly an important factor but Rotes are where aspects of the game really get to shine. If you take a look at a bunch of existing Rotes (outside of the default sphere effects) you'll see several that appear more &quot;powerful&quot; than what you get off of the Damage/Duration/Distance charts, this I believe is deliberately so. Many Rotes have a time factor within them, specific foci that have to be used and so forth and something as a Rote really should be easier and more effectual in it's purpose than something pulled together in the moment.<br /> <br /> In my games I have the -1 Difficulty for Rotes as well as the +1 difficulty for Fast Casting and the space in between for doing stuff you know how to do but have not taken te time to refine into a Rote (or cannot perform the rote for). I also let my players get a little more Bang for their Buck if they take time to create Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T05:23:26-08:00","id":1171509,"title":"","content":"Among other things, rotes tend to have rules. As in, rules-they often have a &quot;system/crunch&quot; section, much like the powers of other splats. And this system usually departs from the general rules of magick.<br /> <br /> I take from that that Rotes don't need to be so restricted by the general rules as fast cast. A Rote, by definition, it's not &quot;fast&quot; nor &quot;improvised&quot;-then it stands to reason that the ST and the player have time to metagame and define a few rules for a rote that don't exist in any manual, much like when you invent a new Thaumaturgy ritual or any new power in any other WoD game (except that, for mages, this is everyday stuff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:18:45-08:00","id":1171589,"title":"","content":"The first question to answer is, &quot;What aspect of magic do I want rotes to exemplify in my game?&quot; They could be signature spells (&quot;Steve's Amazing Laser Punch&quot;), in which case a -1 difficulty makes sense as they're built to perfectly fit their caster's paradigm and are cast regularly. In that case they should also be cheap to buy, because they're more roleplay-based than anything else. It fits a truly reality-warping game because they're based solely on YOU and what your paradigm is. Angie's not going to beg Steve to teach her his Laser Punch because she would need the right Sphere mix anyway, and with that Sphere mix, she can come up with Angie's Amazing Laser Punch much more easily than learning Steve's, and they'll do the same thing.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you might want to have a role for &quot;ancient, powerful magic&quot; in your game. In Mage proper, there's very little reason to go digging in ruins for some dusty spellbook, or to learn the long-forgotten ritual of whatever, because you can do literally everything those effects did simply by wanting to and having the right Spheres. Indeed, the only groups that dig for ancient knowledge, like the Hermetics, do so because their paradigm demands it - they <i>think</i> they need to adhere to the ancient formulae, so they do. So, absent a purely Hermetic game, you could make rotes into rules-stretching effects that <i>cannot</i> be replicated on one's own. So rotes become unique things with unique rules.<br /> <br /> As an example - can anyone with Entropy 4 / Life 2 / Spirit 3 and a decent explanation in their own paradigm go on an Agama-style sojourn in the Low Umbra? Or is that something that only the Euthanatos and their Euthanatos-style ritual can accomplish, thus requiring anyone interested in such a journey to go curry favor with Euthanatoi and learn their paradigm?<br /> <br /> As always, the rules as written contradict themselves: the 1xp per rote implies the former path, while many printed rotes break the Sphere rules in a way that implies the latter. So we get to decide for ourselves and decide what to keep and what to throw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 12-29-2017, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:57:12-08:00","id":1171602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171413#post1171413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the simplest way of doing it, I think. I never really liked that M20 don't give real rules for rotes, since I think they are logical.<br /> <br /> Just as a parallel, take martial arts (or any kind of activity, physical or mental, really). &quot;Rotes&quot; are the things you practiced 'til they became ingrained and you can do them more quickly, reliably and under stress. M20 just doesn't handle that.<br /> <br /> That Mage's magic system's pint is the creativity? Yes, but you could be creative with designing rotes and also with spontaneous casting, if you don't have a handy rote, I don't think it takes away from the creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. If M20 could devote the space it did to Martial Arts maneuvers and Do, it could definitely have devoted some times to an actual game/crunch, non-ad hoc system for Rotes (which, beyond the ill defined -1 Diff is pretty much what is in the game and what everyone is describing that they use). Which is kinda sorta what all the Do crap looked like, with eyes scrunched up tight. As in, &quot;Why do we get a Rote-like system for one thing that one Sect kinda sorta specializes in...&quot; And, if not there, then in BoS or HDYDT, both of which spends scads of words on things that matter tons and tons and TONS less than that echoing abyss filled with random scattered tiny bits of fluff that is the Rote system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T13:01:18-08:00","id":1171606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171481#post1171481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you take a look at a bunch of existing Rotes (outside of the default sphere effects) you'll see several that appear more &quot;powerful&quot; than what you get off of the Damage/Duration/Distance charts, this I believe is deliberately so. Many Rotes have a time factor within them, specific foci that have to be used and so forth and something as a Rote really should be easier and more effectual in it's purpose than something pulled together in the moment..</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we needs rules about this. Why it is so. How it is so. How ST should make up Rotes. What kinds of Rotes NPCs should have. How do PCs come by Rotes (several systems, probably.... though repetition of effect, though study of whatever Rote bank is appropriate to their Sect/Paradigm, etc.)<br /> <br /> And, even then, maybe it's a good idea not to have a rule that says &quot;Here is way to break the rules of the game and make things that are impossible.&quot; Any PC mage worth their salt is going to be pissed that someone can do something with a Rote that they can't do even if they have exactly the same Spheres as is required and shore up their casting rolls with all the bells and whistles. And the only answer is &quot;&lt;Shrug&gt; Just 'cause! It's a Rote!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T13:57:14-08:00","id":1171616,"title":"","content":"I feel like earlier editions of Mage definitely had a much more rules effect to their rotes. This in part is why I like the concept of rotes having special aspects to them than what the charts indicate. I feel it makes rotes more important andand it allows more 'refined' magic to have an effect on the game. One example that comes to mind is the rote Ball of Abyssal Flame in the first OoH Trad book that was basically a nuke. It had a Successx5 multiplier and it made the Forces 5 Prime 5 parts of the spell to have greater damage than the standard Successx2. Another one was in the Dreamspeaker Revised book that allowed the Gauntlet to be reduced to zero at a node despite the official rules for Spirit 2 having a limit to how low you can make the Gauntlet. I like these concepts for rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T15:24:13-08:00","id":1171642,"title":"","content":"I think a little more guidance with Rotes would be a neat idea, however it's not 'Shoring up casting with bells and whistles' it's &quot;Employing the Laws of Reality a given character knows to the greatest of effect&quot;. Just going &quot;I have the right Arete, Spheres and can blag what I'm doing with whats at hand&quot; isn't really using the concept of Paradigm, well it is but it's not how more successful Mages are likely to act. Sure a Hermetic mage may be able to etch the Sign or Mars in the air with a burning stick while speaking three secret words to draw fire from the air and have their enemy combust (as we all know a simple Forces 2 style attack), but a Hermetic mage who has taken the time to acquire a specific wand, keeps it inside a specially treated sheath with gold and red threads all woven in the pattern of Mars Ascending the Heavens and reconsecrates it's power every fortnight is probably employing the secrets of the Order of Hermes in a more successful way.<br /> <br /> The first method of course uses the Damage and Duration charts, doesn't have any Fast Casting penalty because it's a 'basic sphere effect' and can benefit from something like Ritual Casting (Ability to enhance Arete roll) if the ST deems so as well as extended casting rolls etc. <br /> <br /> The second might look a little like the following:<br /> Bolt of Mars' Wrath (Forces 2)<br /> Any novice of the Order of Hermes can turn their knowledge of Forces to brutal effect but those who study the best ways to use Magick in battle (typically those of House Flambeau) study a little deeper to that desire. The mage must procure a wand cut from a lightning struck tree or one that has survived a great fire, they can acquire this themselves as a branch or piece of burnt wood and shape it into their own wand (Dex + Crafts Diff 6). On to this wand must be written or etched enochian words for &quot;Lighting, Wrath and Fire&quot; while it is held for a full day and a full night by the caster within a sacred pentagram (Wits + Ritual/Rites?Appropriate skill for your chronicle roll, Diff 7. A Complete Success (3) or more on this roll lowers the difficulty of the NEXT casting of Bolt of Mars' Wrath by -1). This must be performed once every 12 days or a new wand will be required for the Rote. The wand itself must be kept in a sheath that is marked fore and back with the Sign of Mars and is made of red silk, whenever it is not in use, failure to do so for more than a few minutes will also rob the Rote of it's power. <br /> <br /> The target of a successful Bolt of Mars' Wrath is set on fire suffering damage as calculated by the Dam&amp;Dur chart plus two additional dice. In addition regardless of the subjects actions they will suffer 3 dice of fire damage at the end of their next turn (this includes complete submersion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T05:15:45-08:00","id":1171771,"title":"","content":"Wow, some good stuff in this thread since I last checked it!<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;rotes as ancient magick&quot; is fairly well supported in the setting, what with the idea of certain rituals having been sort of etched into consensual reality through a long history of frequent use, which is why the linear magick of sorcerers works (and doesn't typically incur Paradox). In fact as I've been reading Sorcerer Revised, it occurs to me that one might use the paths and rituals from Sorcerer as rotes in Mage and then either reward them with a -1 difficulty reduction or even say that they don't yield Paradox on a successful casting (might be a little too powerful, I'd have to try it in play).<br /> <br /> It seems to me that these two possible interpretations of rotes are actually fully compatible: they can be signature spells that reduce difficulty by 1 or just remove the fast-casting penalty, or they can be well-established mostly-consensual rituals that don't give Paradox - both types of rote could be used in the same chronicle. As for the third idea of allowing rotes to have greater effects than an improvised spell with the same spheres... it could work if the price is still 1 XP to buy it, but I feel like Mages are quite powerful enough with their current sphere rank limitations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on using Sorcerer rituals as rotes? At least as a narrative conceit - you could still let players invent their own rotes or throw some at them that you've made up yourself, and just say that those are ancient rituals that are also available to sorcerers. Does that seem like an interesting interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T11:51:16-08:00","id":1171842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umsakis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171771#post1171771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are your thoughts on using Sorcerer rituals as rotes? At least as a narrative conceit - you could still let players invent their own rotes or throw some at them that you've made up yourself, and just say that those are ancient rituals that are also available to sorcerers. Does that seem like an interesting interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that idea. I've always been bothered by the disconnect between Sorcerer rules and Mage rules. Especially when for example the fluff of OoH says that they teach their apprentices some Sorcery but it never has an actual effect in the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:27:55-08:00","id":1171853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171642#post1171642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a little more guidance with Rotes would be a neat idea, however it's not 'Shoring up casting with bells and whistles' it's &quot;Employing the Laws of Reality a given character knows to the greatest of effect&quot;. Just going &quot;I have the right Arete, Spheres and can blag what I'm doing with whats at hand&quot; isn't really using the concept of Paradigm, well it is but it's not how more successful Mages are likely to act. Sure a Hermetic mage may be able to etch the Sign or Mars in the air with a burning stick while speaking three secret words to draw fire from the air and have their enemy combust (as we all know a simple Forces 2 style attack), but a Hermetic mage who has taken the time to acquire a specific wand, keeps it inside a specially treated sheath with gold and red threads all woven in the pattern of Mars Ascending the Heavens and reconsecrates it's power every fortnight is probably employing the secrets of the Order of Hermes in a more successful way.<br /> <br /> The first method of course uses the Damage and Duration charts, doesn't have any Fast Casting penalty because it's a 'basic sphere effect' and can benefit from something like Ritual Casting (Ability to enhance Arete roll) if the ST deems so as well as extended casting rolls etc.<br /> <br /> The second might look a little like the following:<br /> Bolt of Mars' Wrath (Forces 2)<br /> Any novice of the Order of Hermes can turn their knowledge of Forces to brutal effect but those who study the best ways to use Magick in battle (typically those of House Flambeau) study a little deeper to that desire. The mage must procure a wand cut from a lightning struck tree or one that has survived a great fire, they can acquire this themselves as a branch or piece of burnt wood and shape it into their own wand (Dex + Crafts Diff 6). On to this wand must be written or etched enochian words for &quot;Lighting, Wrath and Fire&quot; while it is held for a full day and a full night by the caster within a sacred pentagram (Wits + Ritual/Rites?Appropriate skill for your chronicle roll, Diff 7. A Complete Success (3) or more on this roll lowers the difficulty of the NEXT casting of Bolt of Mars' Wrath by -1). This must be performed once every 12 days or a new wand will be required for the Rote. The wand itself must be kept in a sheath that is marked fore and back with the Sign of Mars and is made of red silk, whenever it is not in use, failure to do so for more than a few minutes will also rob the Rote of it's power.<br /> <br /> The target of a successful Bolt of Mars' Wrath is set on fire suffering damage as calculated by the Dam&amp;Dur chart plus two additional dice. In addition regardless of the subjects actions they will suffer 3 dice of fire damage at the end of their next turn (this includes complete submersion).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if the basic premise of &quot;Rotes are just plain BETTER the all other magic&quot; (arguable and the weight of what rules there are bend away from that), we need a LOT more guidance than we get.<br /> <br /> How do you learn that Rote? Does it cost XP? Can a PC come up with such a Rote? Is there an benefit to being a Rote-heavy caster that can be offset by something else that a Rote-FREE caster gets? (Like, say, your Hermetic is weighed down with a shit ton of these Super-Effect Rotes, what about the Ecstatic that pretty much ALWAYS makes up every effect on the spot entirely dependent on the particular circumstances of the situation at hand. <br /> <br /> I don't disagree with the basic premise to some degree. That's sort of how most of the Rotes I've ever written up as a Mage ST have kinda sorta gone (though I usually base what they can do much more concretely on what can be achieved with the constituent Spheres than in making them sort of spells that just do stuff, kinda like Vampire Thaumaturgic Rituals). If you are going to run Rotes this way (and why not? JUST NEED SOME RULES/GUIDANCE ABOUT IT....) I'd probably add in that a botch/Paradox tends to result in a consistent bad result effect. Effectively, Rotes are sort of &quot;grooves&quot; in the surface of Consensual Reality. They work they do because the focused action and intent along with repetition has &quot;worn the groove&quot; and allows for the magic to flow in a particular way.... So there would be additional sections of the write-up. What the associated Paradox would be. But also, the Practice required would be needed, along with the Instruments. Even if you belong to the Sect that uses a Rote, if you aren't doing magic in a particular way, you can't lean on the work of your predecessors to &quot;get in the groove&quot;.<br /> <br /> The silly example of this might be something like an Iteration-X Procedure that has actually become consensual since the 1920s (so, really an IBM Procedure) : <br /> Make Toast (Matter 2)<br /> With construction of the appropriate mechanism, the Scientist is able to turn bread into toast. <br /> Practice: Craftwork, Hypertech?(well, it was back in the 1920's... in which case, maybe Weird Science?) <br /> Instruments: Devices &amp; Mechanisms, Energy (specifically &quot;heat&quot; of some sort)<br /> Paradox: At low levels, a botched casting roll to Make Toast will result in burned toast. Higher levels of Paradox will generally result in the device catching fire and harming the mage, or in creating dangerous electrical shocks. <br /> <br /> So, not just any technomancer can learn this Rote. It would take one with the specified Practices and Instruments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:31:42-08:00","id":1171856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166173-rote-crunch?p=1171842#post1171842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that idea. I've always been bothered by the disconnect between Sorcerer rules and Mage rules. Especially when for example the fluff of OoH says that they teach their apprentices some Sorcery but it never has an actual effect in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've done some dabbling of having Sorcerers be Arete 0 mages who can only do magic by buying Rotes. Though it took some serious caveats and homebrew rules to flesh it out. (E.g. Rotes cost XP. Buying them progressively. How that intersects with buying Spheres. Etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T13:58:06-08:00","id":1172734,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/3491-acolyte-magic\">So have I.</a> As explained in the opening paragraph of the linked post, I like the notion that Sorcery and Magick are very much two different things in the same way that, say, Changeling Arts and Awakened Magick are two different things. That is, sorcery is something that's outside the scope of <b>Mage</b>: it works by its own rules and according to its own principles; and efforts by mages to explain how sorcery is connected to Magick are about as successful as similar efforts to explain why vampires don't suffer Paradox.<br /> <br /> But I can see the benefit of having Sleepers with limited access to Magick through Rotes (\u201cArete 0 mages\u201d, if you will), and the above thread is all about that notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}